🧠 1️⃣7️⃣ Golden Aptitude Strategy

When a percentage question looks complicated:

Step 1

Assume the original value is:

\[
\boxed{100}
\]

Step 2

Apply each percentage change.

Step 3

Compare final value with 100.

Example:

Increase 30%, then decrease 10%.

100
 ↓ +30%
130
 ↓ -10%
117

Therefore:

\[
\boxed{17\%\ increase}
\]

This method is extremely useful.


