🗣️ Communication Practice — 150 Words

Topic: Explaining a Technical Concept Clearly

In a software engineering interview, explaining a concept clearly is as important as knowing the concept. I try to follow a simple structure: first define the concept, then explain why it is needed, and finally give an example. For example, if I explain TCP, I would first say that TCP is a connection-oriented transport protocol. Then I would explain that it provides reliable and ordered delivery using sequence numbers, acknowledgements, and retransmissions. Finally, I would give a practical example such as downloading a file, where losing data can corrupt the result. This structure helps me avoid unnecessary technical details and makes my explanation easier to understand. I also try to speak slowly and confidently instead of rushing through the answer. My goal is not to use complicated words, but to demonstrate that I genuinely understand the concept.

